# Read by BuildKit in preference to a .dockerignore at the context root, which is
# what lets this service own its exclusions while building from the repository
# root (see the header of Dockerfile).
#
# The context is the whole repository, so this is subtractive: everything the
# build does not need, plus everything that must never enter an image.

# Never in an image. The gateway has no private key, but the pattern stays so a
# copy of one can never ride along by accident.
**/keys/private.pem
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
http/http-client.private.env.json

# Build output — would be shipped to the daemon and invalidate the cache on
# every local build.
**/target/
docker-data/
.logs/
*.log

# Not part of any build.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.idea/
.vscode/
*.iml
docs/
http/
sd/
config/
compose.yml
**/Dockerfile
**/Dockerfile.dockerignore
**/.dockerignore

# Other modules. mugen-gateway needs the parent pom and shared/, and nothing else —
# except every sibling's pom.xml, because the parent pom lists them all as
# modules and Maven refuses to read a reactor with a module directory missing,
# -pl or not. A pom alone is enough for it to be "present".
eureka-server/
services/*
!services/*/pom.xml
!services/mugen-gateway/
